Parts by another author

The Felt look in shell/platform/web (the Felt parts of pangea.css, pangea.js, mapping.js,
host.js, builder.js and harmony.js, as the first line of each says) and six examples (the whole
of the logic.cpp of shell/examples/bass-and-drums, hands-and-drums, pocket-drums,
ostinato-hands, rolling-line and two-hands, with two-hands' README.md and test folder) are not
Conduit AI's code. Since 25 November 2026 their author offers them, as they are in this
repository, under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later, as well as under
his own licence, at your choice: shell/platform/web/FELT-LICENSE.md has both, and each of the
six logic.cpp says so. Five of them also carry the MIDI shelf's licence line, which names
library/midi/LICENSE.md, in Pangea's own repository only; its text is the first part of
shell/platform/web/FELT-LICENSE.md. So all the code in this repository may be used under the GNU
Affero General Public License.

