Third parties in the desktop app

- Faust 2.88.0, by GRAME. A packaged app carries the compiler, built by desktop/scripts/build-faust.sh
  from GRAME's release without changes, under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later,
  with its complete source; and its headers and libraries, under the GNU Lesser General Public
  License, version 2.1 or later, with the Faust exception, each library function as it says.
  Nothing of Faust is in this repository: the script downloads it and checks its SHA-256.
- Ninja 1.13.2. A packaged app carries the release binary, under the Apache License 2.0, with its
  licence text. Not in this repository.
- CMake 3.31.12, by Kitware (BSD 3-Clause), and JUCE 8.0.10: the app downloads each from its
  maker's release on the member's Mac and checks its SHA-256. Neither is in this repository or in
  the app.
- The app's Rust crates (desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.lock) and JavaScript packages
  (desktop/pnpm-lock.yaml) are fetched when it is built, each under its own licence: MIT, Apache
  2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode 3.0, the Unlicense, CC0 and MPL 2.0. The MPL 2.0 comes through
  Tauri's Rust crates (cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext and selectors), which
  are in the app, and through the JavaScript build tools (lightningcss, by way of Vite), which only
  build the page and are not shipped in the app. All of these can be combined with the GNU Affero
  General Public License, version 3.
